  "term": "psychiatric classification",
  "definition": "In mental health, psychiatric classification refers to the systems used to organize and diagnose mental disorders, such as DSM-5-TR. In the source, these systems are described as largely categorical, relying on symptom clusters and diagnostic thresholds, while newer dimensional models aim to capture cross-cutting processes across disorders.",
